@startuml OXPAID Update Duplication Analysis
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

title **CRITICAL DEVIATION: OXPAID Updated in 4 Locations**

skinparam package {
    BackgroundColor<<violation>> #FFCCCC
    BorderColor<<violation>> #FF0000
    BackgroundColor<<ok>> #CCFFCC
    BorderColor<<ok>> #00AA00
}

package "Expected Architecture" <<ok>> {
    rectangle "Single OrderPaymentStateService" as expected {
        rectangle "updatePaidTimestamp()" as single
    }
}

package "Actual Implementation" <<violation>> {
    rectangle "StripeOrderCreationHandler.php\nLines 160-193" as loc1 {
        note right: Uses PHP date()\n"Primary path"
    }

    rectangle "OrderPaymentCompletedHandler.php\nLines 76-115" as loc2 {
        note right: Uses MySQL NOW()\n"Event-driven backup"
    }

    rectangle "PaymentIntentSucceededHandler.php\nLines 128-136" as loc3 {
        note right: Uses Stripe timestamp\n"Webhook handler"
    }

    rectangle "WebhookProcessingService.php\nLines 948-1025" as loc4 {
        note right: Uses DatabaseProvider\n"Legacy path"
    }
}

database "oxorder.OXPAID" as db

expected -[hidden]down-> loc1

loc1 --> db : **Inconsistent**\nDate Handling
loc2 --> db
loc3 --> db
loc4 --> db

note bottom of db
    **Problems:**
    1. Four different date sources (PHP, MySQL NOW(), Stripe)
    2. Race conditions between handlers
    3. Different lookup strategies (OXID vs OXTRANSID)
    4. Different DB access methods
end note

@enduml
